      "interpretation": "After original arrivals cease, q(next)=(1+beta)*max(0,q-mu), with unstable boundary mu*(1+beta)/beta. Compression plus delay-generated work can keep a stop disposition queue growing in this stipulated fluid model. Remove the return edge or provision burst capacity and the adverse persistence disappears. This is inherited queue mathematics, not a new theorem or empirical result.",
      "counterexample": "Uniform earlier time shifts do not compress arrivals. Bounded follow-on obligations, spare disposition capacity, or independent reconciliation can remove persistence.",
      "safety_limit": "All local stops are honored immediately. Continued counterparty obligations are not continued AI execution. No immediate safety cost is modeled and slower safety shutdowns are not recommended."
